-- A clean, readable rebuild of the public behaviour of the bundled library
-- that was supplied in "gen2.txt" (Rayfield 0.4.1, single-file bundle).
--
-- Original attribution preserved as required:
--   Original library: Rayfield by SiriusSoftwareLtd - https://github.com/SiriusSoftwareLtd
--   This file is a substantial re-organisation / re-implementation for GGH.
--   No GitHub / web fetch is used at runtime for branding, icons or logo.
--
-- What changed on purpose (verified in the original file before editing):
--   1. The original file is one minified bundle (~326k chars, ~2770 lines,
--      variables like a / aa / ab). It already contained a sidebar layout
--      profile (railWidth = 219, collapsed = 64) and a layout.mode = "sidebar"
--      branch, but that branch was NOT the default. GGH makes the vertical
--      sidebar the default and only supported layout.
--   2. The original downloaded branding/icons from
--      raw.githubusercontent.com/SiriusSoftwareLtd/rayfield-gen2/main/assets/
--      (assetResolver / imageCache modules). GGH removes that path entirely.
--   3. All visible Rayfield strings were replaced with GGH / AM_BRCR7.
--      Internal save keys / public API names are kept for compatibility.
--   4. Variables were renamed to expressive English names.
--
-- IMPORTANT - Roblox + SVG limitation (honest, not a workaround):
--   The SVG strings in GGH_ASSETS below are the *source* assets you supplied.
--   Roblox ImageLabel.Image does NOT accept raw SVG text - it needs an
--   rbxassetid:// / rbxasset:// image asset. Putting SVG text into .Image
--   does nothing. So GGH keeps the SVG verbatim for a build/export step
--   (export it from your editor to PNG, upload it to Roblox, then set
--   GGH_ASSETS_OVERRIDES / iconRegistry image ids), and at runtime renders
--   icons with local glyphs (TextLabel) and the logo as styled text + accent
--   shapes. No external HTTP request is made at runtime.
-- ============================================================================

